# Delete safety (user data)

Deleting user files is irreversible risk. Treat every delete path as safety-critical.

## Must hold

1. **Select-only** — remove only paths in the explicit user-confirmed delete set. Never “delete the other duplicates in the group” unless each path was selected.
2. **Never delete keep-candidates** — keep set and delete set must be disjoint; assert before acting.
3. **TOCTOU re-verify** — immediately before each remove, re-check canonical real path + size + content hash (and device/inode when available) against the scan record. Any mismatch → **skip**, log failure, continue others.
4. **Path allowlist** — resolved path must stay under an approved scan root; reject symlink retargets and `..` escapes.
5. **Two-phase UX** — dry-run/preview of exact paths, then explicit confirm, then per-file results (deleted / skipped / failed). No silent bulk success.
6. **Trash default** — OS trash/recycle; permanent delete only behind a separate confirmation.
7. **Fail closed** — on any doubt, do not delete.
8. **Audit** — every attempt (success/skip/fail) recorded without file contents.

## Tests required before shipping delete

- Hash mismatch after scan → skip
- Symlink swapped to another file → skip
- Keep-candidate in delete set → reject entire batch or that entry
- Path outside scan root → reject
- Partial failures leave a clear report; remaining selected files still processed safely

Do not mark a delete-related slice done until these UAT cases are green.
